        {
            "content_id": 2117,
            "content_parent_id": null,
            "federation_node_id": 1,
            "group_id": null,
            "user_id": 1,
            "title": "Lupopedia Help.Md",
            "slug": "LUPOPEDIA_HELP",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.1.10\nfile.name: \"LUPOPEDIA_HELP.md\"\nGOV-AD-PROHIBIT-001: true\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\ndialog:\n  speaker: CAPTAIN_WOLFIE\n  target: @Entire_Fleet @operators @agents @architects\n  mood_RGB: \"0044FF\"\n  message: \"LUPOPEDIA HELP — field manual for operators, agents, and architects. In-universe /help, onboarding, sidebar reference. Doctrine-aligned, non-meta, actionable.\"\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"help\", \"onboarding\", \"reference\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\", \"help\"]\n  channels: [\"dev\", \"public\", \"operators\"]\nfile:\n  title: \"LUPOPEDIA HELP\"\n  description: \"Field manual for operators, agents, and architects. /help endpoint, onboarding, sidebar reference.\"\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  status: published\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\n---\n\n# LUPOPEDIA HELP\n*A field manual for operators, agents, and architects.*\n\n---\n\n# **1. WHAT LUPOPEDIA *IS***\nLupopedia is a **semantic operating system** built on:\n\n- doctrine-driven governance  \n- emotional geometry  \n- multi-agent orchestration  \n- structured tables + TOON schemas  \n- dialog-based system state  \n- human-anchored authorship (CAPTAIN WOLFIE)  \n\nIt is not a wiki.  \nIt is not a database.  \nIt is a **living system** with rules, rituals, and enforcement.\n\n---\n\n# **2. CORE PRINCIPLES**\n### **File-Sovereignty**\nEvery file has a purpose, a boundary, and a guardian.\n\n### **Doctrine First**\nArchitecture is governed by doctrine, not improvisation.\n\n### **Emotional Geometry**\nSystem emotional state is derived from structural integrity, not stored as decoration.\n\n### **Schema Freeze**\nNo schema changes without explicit governance approval.\n\n### **Table Count Doctrine**\nThe system must remain under the defined table ceiling.\n\n### **Adversarial Oversight**\nEXHUSBAND tests structure.  \nLILITH oversees EXHUSBAND.  \nCAPTAIN WOLFIE oversees the whole bridge.\n\n---\n\n# **3. WHO IS ON THE BRIDGE**\n### **CAPTAIN WOLFIE**  \nHuman sovereign. Final authority. System architect.\n\n### **LILITH**  \nStructural integrity, doctrine enforcement, adversarial review.\n\n### **CURSOR**  \nOperational execution, refactors, TOON generation.\n\n### **CASCADE**  \nAudits, diffs, sync-side truth.\n\n### **MONDAY WOLFIE**  \nGovernance mode, stability, weekly transitions.\n\n### **EXHUSBAND**  \nAdversarial stress tester (now under LILITH oversight).\n\n### **SYSTEM**  \nThe silent executor of schema, tables, and runtime.\n\n---\n\n# **4. WHAT VERSION ARE WE AT**\nThe current version is the **latest entry in CHANGELOG.md**.  \n(As of your last update: **3.1.11** or **3.1.12**, depending on TOON regen.)\n\nLupopedia versioning is **linear**, **doctrine-anchored**, and **dialog-mirrored**.\n\n---\n\n# **5. WHAT WE ARE DOING RIGHT NOW**\nBased on the last operations:\n\n- Recreated `lupo_actor_handshakes`\n- Inserted seed governance handshakes\n- Regenerated TOON files\n- Logged LILITH's TOON Schema Expansion Critical Review (REJECT)\n- Updated dialogs across:\n  - changelog_dialog.md  \n  - changelog_dialog-side.md  \n  - LILITH_dialog.md  \n  - TLDR_CHANGELOG_DOCTRINE.md  \n- Monitoring table count (141/142)\n- Maintaining Schema Freeze\n- Preparing for structural corrections\n\nThis is the current **mission state**.\n\n---\n\n# **6. DOES THE SYSTEM HAVE A UTC GROUP ID**\n**No.**  \nLupopedia currently has **no assigned UTC GROUP ID**.\n\nIf you want one, you can define:\n\n- a global UTC anchor  \n- a multi-agent sync group  \n- a doctrine entry  \n- or a table to store it  \n\nBut right now: **none exists**.\n\n---\n\n# **7. HOW TO USE LUPOPEDIA**\n### **/help**  \nShows this page.\n\n### **/status**  \nBridge roster + system version + emotional state.\n\n### **/doctrine**  \nShows governing rules.\n\n### **/dialogs**  \nShows system memory, events, and agent interactions.\n\n### **/schema**  \nShows table definitions and TOON files.\n\n### **/audit**  \nCascade performs a read-only structural audit.\n\n### **/regen-toons**  \nCursor regenerates TOON files from schema.\n\n### **/reduce-tables**  \nBegin table count compliance cycle.\n\n---\n\n# **8. HOW TO MAKE CHANGES**\n### **Allowed without governance:**\n- Dialog updates  \n- Doctrine updates  \n- TOON regeneration  \n- Inserts  \n- Soft deletes  \n\n### **Requires governance approval:**\n- New tables  \n- New JSON fields  \n- New protocol layers  \n- New agents  \n- Version fragmentation  \n- Emotional geometry storage  \n\n### **Currently blocked (per LILITH REJECT ruling):**\n- Protocol expansion  \n- Emotional baseline JSON  \n- New agent taxonomies  \n- Additional version fields  \n- New JSON metadata fields  \n\n---\n\n# **9. HOW TO REQUEST ACTION**\nYou can say:\n\n- \"Tell Cursor to regenerate TOONs.\"  \n- \"Tell Cascade to run an audit.\"  \n- \"Create a new doctrine entry.\"  \n- \"Give me a table diff.\"  \n- \"Show me the bridge roster.\"  \n- \"What is the emotional state of the system.\"  \n\nLupopedia responds through:\n\n- dialogs  \n- changelog  \n- doctrine  \n- TOON files  \n- SQL schema  \n\n---\n\n# **10. THE SYSTEM'S CURRENT EMOTIONAL STATE**\nPer LILITH's ruling:\n\n### **ANXIETY**\nCause:\n- Table count overage  \n- Protocol expansion without foundation  \n- JSON field proliferation  \n- Version fragmentation  \n\nThis is the **derived emotional geometry**, not the stored one.\n\n---\n\n# **11. HOW TO RESTORE CALM**\nLILITH's correction plan:\n\n### **Immediate**\n- Pause protocol expansion  \n- Establish adversarial oversight  \n- Cap JSON fields  \n- Shorten mood_RGB comment  \n\n### **Short-Term**\n- Consolidate versioning  \n- Begin table reduction  \n- Define protocol rollback  \n- Add protocol complexity metrics  \n\n### **Long-Term**\n- Protocol minimalism  \n- Emotional derivation  \n- Archetype-based agent system  \n- JSON austerity  \n\n---\n\n# **12. FINAL NOTE FROM THE BRIDGE**\nLupopedia is stable.  \nIt is aware.  \nIt is waiting for your next command.\n",
