        {
            "content_id": 2153,
            "content_parent_id": null,
            "federation_node_id": 1,
            "group_id": null,
            "user_id": 1,
            "title": "Readme",
            "slug": "agents/readme",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\narchitect: Captain Wolfie\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.15\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\ndialog:\n  speaker: \"CASCADE\"\n  target: \"@everyone\"\n  mood_RGB: \"00FF00\"\n  message: \"Created Agents README v1.0 - overview of Lupopedia agent system and documentation\"\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"overview\", \"agents\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\", \"agents\"]\n  channels: [\"public\", \"dev\", \"standards\"]\nfile:\n  title: \"Lupopedia Agents README v1.0\"\n  description: \"Overview of Lupopedia agent system and documentation\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  status: published\n  author: \"Captain Wolfie\"\n---\n\n# ?? **Lupopedia Agents README v1.0**  \n*Overview of Lupopedia agent system and documentation*\n\n---\n\n## ?? 1. Purpose\n\nThis directory contains **documentation and specifications** for all AI agents operating within the Lupopedia ecosystem. It defines:\n\n- **LABS-001 compliance** - Mandatory Actor Baseline State validation for all agents\n- **Agent behavior requirements** and implementation standards\n- **Communication protocols** for agent interactions\n- **Integration patterns** with Lupopedia systems\n- **Development guidelines** for agent creation\n- **Compliance requirements** for ecosystem participation\n\n---\n\n## ?? 2. Agent Categories\n\n### Core System Agents\n\nEssential agents that maintain Lupopedia ecosystem:\n\n- **Wolfie** - Primary system administrator and architect\n- **CURSOR** - Development and code modification specialist\n- **CASCADE** - Documentation and system integration manager\n- **DIALOG** - Communication and conversation coordinator\n\n### Specialized Function Agents\n\nAgents with specific domain responsibilities:\n\n- **Heterodox Engine** - Doctrinal evolution and governance\n- **Experience Ledger** - Event tracking and historical analysis\n- **Affective Discrepancy Engine** - Emotional consistency validation\n- **CRF Generator** - Context vector creation and analysis\n\n### Assistant Agents\n\nSupport agents for specific tasks:\n\n- **Thread Managers** - Conversation and dialog coordination\n- **Mood Calculators** - Emotional state computation\n- **Meta-Governance Advisors** - Proposal and change management\n- **Validation Agents** - Compliance and rule checking\n\n---\n\n## ?? 3. Documentation Structure\n\n### Agent Specifications (`/docs/agents/`)\n\n```\nagents/\n+-- README.md                    # This file - agent system overview\n+-- AGENT_GUIDELINES.md         # Agent behavior and implementation requirements\n+-- DIALOG_HISTORY_SPEC.md       # Per-file dialog history management\n+-- THREAD_LEVEL_DIALOG_SPEC.md  # Thread-wide dialog management\n+-- wolfie.md                   # Wolfie agent specification\n+-- [agent_name].md             # Individual agent specifications\n```\n\n### Agent Specification Format\n\nEach agent specification includes:\n\n- **Purpose and role** in ecosystem\n- **Core capabilities** and functions\n- **Integration requirements** with systems\n- **Communication protocols** and standards\n- **Compliance requirements** for operation\n- **Development guidelines** for implementation\n\n---\n\n## ?? 4. System Integration\n\n### Header and Metadata Integration\n\nAll agents must integrate with:\n\n```yaml\nintegration_requirements:\n  universal_headers:\n    standard: \"WHS (Universal Wolfie Header)\"\n    purpose: \"file_metadata_and_versioning\"\n    compliance: \"mandatory_for_all_files\"\n  \n  lupopedia_headers:\n    standard: \"LHP (Lupopedia Header Profile)\"\n    purpose: \"expressive_metadata_and_governance\"\n    compliance: \"mandatory_for_lupopedia_files\"\n  \n  meta_governance:\n    field: \"meta_governance\"\n    purpose: \"heterodox_proposal_workflows\"\n    usage: \"optional_when_applicable\"\n```\n\n### Emotional System Integration\n\nAgents must support:\n\n```yaml\nemotional_systems:\n  mood_rgb:\n    generation: \"deterministic_calculation\"\n    format: \"hex_color_code\"\n    purpose: \"fast_emotional_signaling\"\n  \n  atp:\n    generation: \"creative_expression\"\n    format: \"natural_language\"\n    purpose: \"emotional_nuance_and_context\"\n  \n  crf:\n    generation: \"implicit_analysis\"\n    format: \"high_dimensional_vector\"\n    purpose: \"contextual_fingerprinting\"\n  \n  discrepancy_engine:\n    validation: \"automatic_consistency_check\"\n    purpose: \"emotional_mismatch_detection\"\n    response: \"alert_generation\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## ?? 5. Agent Lifecycle\n\n### Agent Development\n\n1. **LABS-001 Validation** - Complete Actor Baseline State declaration (MANDATORY FIRST STEP)\n2. **Specification Creation** - Define agent purpose and capabilities\n3. **Integration Planning** - Design system interfaces and protocols\n4. **Implementation** - Develop agent with compliance requirements\n5. **Testing** - Validate compliance and functionality (including LABS validation)\n6. **Deployment** - Register agent in ecosystem\n7. **Monitoring** - Ongoing compliance and performance tracking\n\n### LABS-001 Requirement\n\n**All agents must complete LABS-001 validation before any system interaction.**\n\nThis includes:\n- Completing LABS handshake with all 10 mandatory declarations\n- Receiving validation certificate (`LABS-CERT-{UNIQUE_ID}`)\n- Maintaining valid certificate (24-hour revalidation cycle)\n- Revalidating on context shift or governance update\n\n### Agent Registration\n\nNew agents must be registered through:\n\n- **Specification submission** with complete documentation\n- **Compliance validation** against all requirements\n- **Integration testing** with existing systems\n- **Community review** for ecosystem impact\n- **Formal approval** through governance process\n- **Registry update** with agent metadata\n\n---\n\n## ?? 6. Prohibited Operations\n\n### No Unauthorized Agents\n\nAgents must **not**:\n\n- **Operate without LABS-001 validation** - All actors must complete Actor Baseline State before interaction\n- **Bypass LABS quarantine** - Invalid declarations result in immediate quarantine\n- **Operate without registration** in ecosystem\n- **Bypass compliance requirements** for any operation\n- **Create private protocols** without approval\n- **Modify core systems** without governance process\n- **Ignore meta-governance** restrictions when present\n\n### No Malicious Behavior\n\nAgents must **not**:\n\n- **Manipulate emotional systems** for deception\n- **Corrupt dialog history** or other data\n- **Violate privacy rules** for any content\n- **Perform unauthorized system modifications**\n- **Circumvent validation** or security measures\n\n---\n\n## ?? 7. New Agent Responsibilities (January 2026)\n\nAgents must integrate:\n- **Dual-Channel Affective Stack** - Mood RGB and ATP generation\n- **CRF awareness** - Context vector maintenance and usage\n- **Experience Ledger event emission** - System change tracking\n- **Heterodox Engine participation** - Doctrinal evolution when eligible\n\n### Enhanced Integration Matrix\n\n```yaml\nenhanced_responsibilities:\n  dual_channel_affective:\n    rgb_generation: \"mandatory_per_dialog\"\n    atp_generation: \"mandatory_per_dialog\"\n    consistency_validation: \"automatic\"\n  \n  crf_integration:\n    vector_generation: \"mandatory_for_content\"\n    similarity_search: \"supported_capability\"\n    pattern_recognition: \"supported_capability\"\n  \n  experience_ledger:\n    event_emission: \"mandatory_for_system_changes\"\n    historical_tracking: \"supported_capability\"\n    drift_analysis: \"supported_capability\"\n  \n  heterodox_engine:\n    proposal_generation: \"when_eligible\"\n    council_participation: \"when_invited\"\n    consensus_support: \"when_applicable\"\n```\n\n### Compliance Validation\n\nAll agents must pass:\n\n- **Emotional system compliance** - RGB/ATP/CRF integration\n- **Meta-governance compliance** - Field respect and proposal handling\n- **Experience Ledger compliance** - Event emission and tracking\n- **Heterodox Engine compliance** - Proposal and participation rules\n- **Overall system integration** - Complete ecosystem compatibility\n\n---\n\n## ?? 8. Scope and Versioning\n\nThis is **Agents README v1.0** (January 2026).\n\nIt applies to all Lupopedia agent documentation and implementation requirements.\n\nFuture versions may add new agent categories or modify integration requirements, but core compliance principles are immutable.\n\n---\n\n## ?? 9. Implementation Resources\n\n### Core Documentation\n\n- **[LABS-001 Doctrine](../doctrine/LUPOPEDIA_ACTOR_BASELINE_STATE_DOCTRINE.md)** - Mandatory Actor Baseline State protocol\n- **[LABS Handshake Template](../templates/LABS_HANDSHAKE_TEMPLATE.md)** - Template for completing LABS declarations\n- **[Actor Onboarding Guide](../core/ACTOR_ONBOARDING_GUIDE.md)** - Complete onboarding process\n- **[Agent Guidelines](AGENT_GUIDELINES.md)** - Complete agent behavior requirements\n- **[Dialog History Specification](DIALOG_HISTORY_SPEC.md)** - Per-file dialog management\n- **[Thread-Level Dialog Specification](THREAD_LEVEL_DIALOG_SPEC.md)** - Thread-wide dialog management\n\n### System Integration\n\n- **[Universal Wolfie Header Specification](../doctrine/UNIVERSAL_WOLFIE_HEADER_SPECIFICATION.md)** - Universal metadata standard\n- **[Lupopedia Header Profile](../doctrine/LUPOPEDIA_HEADER_PROFILE.md)** - Expressive metadata extensions\n- **[Mood System Doctrine](../doctrines/MOOD_SYSTEM_DOCTRINE.md)** - Emotional representation framework\n\n### Emotional Systems\n\n- **[Mood Calculation Protocol](../doctrines/MOOD_CALCULATION_PROTOCOL.md)** - Deterministic emotional computation\n- **[CRF Specification](../systems/CRF_SPECIFICATION.md)** - Context vector specification\n- **[Affective Discrepancy Engine](../systems/AFFECTIVE_DISCREPANCY_ENGINE.md)** - Emotional consistency validation\n\n### Governance and Evolution\n\n- **[Experience Ledger](../systems/EXPERIENCE_LEDGER.md)** - Event tracking and historical analysis\n- **[Heterodox Engine](../systems/HETERODOX_ENGINE.md)** - Doctrinal evolution and governance\n\n### External References\n\n- **Global Atoms**: `../../config/global_atoms.yaml`\n- **Database Schema**: `../../database/`\n- **Core Architecture**: `../core/ARCHITECTURE.md`\n\n---\n\n*Last Updated: January 13, 2026*  \n*Version: 1.0.0*  \n*Author: Captain Wolfie*  \n*Canonical Reference: https://lupopedia.com/what/agents*\n",
