            "user_id": 1,
            "title": "Wolfie",
            "slug": "appendix/wolfie",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\narchitect: Captain Wolfie\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.15\ndialog:\n  speaker: CURSOR\n  target: @everyone\n  message: \"Created wolfie.md: Wolfie's lived context - addiction, jail, rehab, loss, mythic study. Lupopedia is the system he wished he had when everything fell apart: holds conflicting claims, evidence, context without dogma or nihilism.\"\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"people\", \"biography\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\"]\n  channels: [\"public\", \"dev\"]\nin_this_file_we_have:\n  - Lived context\n  - Role in Lupopedia\n  - Why the system exists\nfile:\n  title: \"Who is Wolfie\"\n  description: \"Wolfie is the mythic and working name of Eric Robin Gerdes, creator and steward of Lupopedia. His lived context shaped the system's architecture and doctrine.\"\n  version: \"3.0.0\"\n  status: published\n  author: \"Captain Wolfie\"\n---\n\n# Who is Wolfie\n\n\"Wolfie\" is the mythic and working name of Eric Robin Gerdes, the original creator and ongoing steward of Lupopedia.\n\n## Lived context\n\nWolfie did not design Lupopedia from an ivory tower. The system comes out of:\n\n- the death of his wife\n- years of addiction, bad habits, and destructive choices\n- 17 months in jail\n- 10 months in rehab\n- another marriage lost through his own actions\n- deep exposure to \"how not to live\"\n\nAfter getting sober, he spent years studying patterns in human belief and narrative, including 22+ different religions and myth systems. The goal was not to become a preacher, but to understand:\n\n- how humans construct \"truth\"\n- how errors, distortions, and comforting stories accumulate\n- how resilience, optimism, and integrity are actually built\n\n## Role in Lupopedia\n\nWolfie is:\n\n- the **digital archaeologist** of the old Crafty Syntax system\n- the **architect** of the new semantic OS\n- the **mythic persona** guiding agents like Thoth and Lilith\n- the one insisting on strong doctrine, clear boundaries, and explicit documentation\n\nLupopedia is not a religious project. It is the system Wolfie wishes he had when everything fell apart: something that can hold conflicting claims, evidence, and context without collapsing into dogma or nihilism.\n\nThat is why the schema is strict, the table count is disciplined, and the agents are named with symbolic weight. This isn't just software; it's a way of refusing to lie to ourselves about how knowledge and experience actually work.\n\n",
