            "user_id": 1,
            "title": "Wolfie Header Global Atoms Guide",
            "slug": "dev/wolfie_header_global_atoms_guide",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\narchitect: Captain Wolfie\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.14\ndialog:\n  speaker: CURSOR\n  target: @everyone\n  message: \"Created guide for using global atoms to avoid version number search/replace across all files.\"\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\nfile:\n  title: \"WOLFIE Header Global Atoms Usage Guide\"\n  description: \"How to use global atoms to avoid search/replace across all files when version numbers change\"\n  version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  status: published\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"development\", \"guide\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\", \"dev\"]\n  channels: [\"dev\"]\nin_this_file_we_have:\n  - What Are Global Atoms\n  - Why Use Global Atoms\n  - Available Global Atoms\n  - How to Use Global Atoms in WOLFIE Headers\n  - How to Update Version Numbers\n  - Examples\nfile_atoms:\n  FILE_GUIDE_TYPE: \"usage-guide\"\n---\n\n# ?? **WOLFIE Header Global Atoms Usage Guide**\n\n## **What Are Global Atoms?**\n\nGlobal atoms are **symbolic references** defined in `/config/global_atoms.yaml` that can be used in any WOLFIE header instead of hardcoding values like version numbers, author names, or copyright strings.\n\n**Purpose:** Prevent the need to search/replace version numbers across dozens of files when Lupopedia is upgraded.\n\n---\n\n## **Why Use Global Atoms?**\n\nWhen Lupopedia upgrades from `3.0.1` to `3.0.2`, instead of:\n\n? **Manually searching and replacing `\"3.0.1\"` in dozens of files**\n\nYou can:\n\n? **Update ONE file** (`config/global_atoms.yaml`)  \n? **All WOLFIE headers automatically use the new version**  \n? **No file-by-file search/replace needed**\n\n---\n\n## **Available Global Atoms**\n\nAll global atoms are defined in `/config/global_atoms.yaml`. Current available atoms:\n\n### **Version Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION` — Current Lupopedia version (currently `\"3.0.1\"`)\n\n### **Author Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS` — Primary author name (currently `\"Captain Wolfie\"`)\n\n### **Copyright Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_CURRENT_COPYRIGHT` — Copyright string (currently `\"© 2025-2026 Eric Robin Gerdes. All rights reserved.\"`)\n\n### **Year Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_CURRENT_YEAR` — Current year (currently `\"2026\"`)\n\n### **Project Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_PROJECT_NAME` — Project name (currently `\"Lupopedia\"`)\n\n### **Status Atoms**\n- `GLOBAL_DEFAULT_STATUS` — Default file status (currently `\"published\"`)\n\n### **Complex Atoms** (referenced with dot notation in documentation)\n- `GLOBAL_LUPOPEDIA_COMPANY_STRUCTURE` — Company structure and team information\n- `GLOBAL_LUPOPEDIA_V4_0_2_CORE_AGENTS` — Required agents list for v3.0.2\n\n---\n\n## **How to Use Global Atoms in WOLFIE Headers**\n\n### **Step 1: Reference the Atom in `header_atoms:` Block**\n\nList all global atoms you're using in the `header_atoms:` block:\n\n```yaml\n---\nwolfie.headers.version: 3.0.1\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\n---\n```\n\n### **Step 2: Use the Atom Name (Not the Value) in `file:` Block**\n\nUse the literal atom name (not resolver syntax) in your file metadata:\n\n```yaml\nfile:\n  version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\n  status: GLOBAL_DEFAULT_STATUS\n```\n\n**Important:** Use the atom name exactly as written (e.g., `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION`), not the value (not `\"3.0.1\"`).\n\n---\n\n## **Complete Example**\n\n### **? CORRECT: Using Global Atoms**\n\n```yaml\n---\nwolfie.headers.version: 3.0.1\ndialog:\n  speaker: CURSOR\n  target: @everyone\n  message: \"Updated documentation with new agent information.\"\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\nfile:\n  title: \"Agent Guide\"\n  description: \"Guide to Lupopedia AI agents\"\n  version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  status: published\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"agents\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\"]\n  channels: [\"dev\", \"public\"]\n---\n```\n\n### **? WRONG: Hardcoding Values**\n\n```yaml\n---\nwolfie.headers.version: 3.0.1\nfile:\n  version: \"3.0.1\"  # ? Hardcoded - will need search/replace on upgrade\n  author: \"Captain Wolfie\"  # ? Hardcoded - will need search/replace if author changes\n---\n```\n\n---\n\n## **How to Update Version Numbers**\n\nWhen Lupopedia upgrades from `3.0.1` to `3.0.2`:\n\n### **Step 1: Update `/config/global_atoms.yaml`**\n\n```yaml\n# Change this line:\nGLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION: \"3.0.1\"\n\n# To this:\nGLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION: \"3.0.2\"\n```\n\n### **Step 2: That's It!**\n\nAll WOLFIE headers that reference `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION` will now automatically use `\"3.0.2\"` when resolved.\n\n**No search/replace needed across any files.**\n\n---\n\n## **Resolution Process**\n\nWhen a tool or agent reads a WOLFIE header:\n\n1. **Detects atom reference** — Sees `version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION`\n2. **Resolves atom** — Looks up `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION` in `/config/global_atoms.yaml`\n3. **Gets value** — Retrieves `\"3.0.1\"` (or whatever the current value is)\n4. **Uses resolved value** — Treats `version` as `\"3.0.1\"` for processing\n\n**The file itself still contains the symbolic reference.**  \n**Only during resolution does the actual value get substituted.**\n\n---\n\n## **Cursor Behavior Rules**\n\nCursor (and all IDEs) must:\n\n- ? **Preserve symbolic references** — Keep `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION` exactly as written\n- ? **Resolve values when reading** — Look up actual value from `global_atoms.yaml` when processing\n- ? **List atoms in `header_atoms:`** — Declare all global atoms used in the file\n- ? **NEVER expand atoms** — Don't replace `GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION` with `\"3.0.1\"` in the file\n- ? **NEVER inline values** — Don't substitute the actual value when writing headers\n- ? **NEVER modify `global_atoms.yaml`** — Unless explicitly instructed to update version\n\n---\n\n## **Benefits**\n\n1. **Single Source of Truth** — Version number defined once in `global_atoms.yaml`\n2. **No Search/Replace** — Update one file, all headers automatically use new version\n3. **Consistency** — All files guaranteed to reference the same version\n4. **Maintainability** — Easy to update version across entire codebase\n5. **Symbolic Clarity** — Clear that this is a reference, not a hardcoded value\n\n---\n\n## **Migration Strategy**\n\nWhen migrating existing files to use global atoms:\n\n1. **Add `header_atoms:` block** — List all global atoms you'll use\n2. **Replace hardcoded values** — Change `version: \"3.0.1\"` to `version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION`\n3. **Test resolution** — Verify tools can resolve the atoms correctly\n4. **Update documentation** — Document that files now use atoms\n\n**Example Migration:**\n\n**Before:**\n```yaml\nfile:\n  version: \"3.0.1\"\n  author: \"Captain Wolfie\"\n```\n\n**After:**\n```yaml\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\nfile:\n  version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Reference Documentation**\n\n- **WOLFIE Header Specification:** [WOLFIE_HEADER_SPECIFICATION.md](../agents/WOLFIE_HEADER_SPECIFICATION.md)\n- **Global Atoms File:** `/config/global_atoms.yaml`\n- **Atom Resolution Order:** See WOLFIE_HEADER_SPECIFICATION.md section 7\n\n---\n\n**Remember:** The power of global atoms is that you **update once, use everywhere**. No more hunting through dozens of files to update version numbers.\n",
