        {
            "content_id": 2318,
            "content_parent_id": null,
            "federation_node_id": 1,
            "group_id": null,
            "user_id": 1,
            "title": "Jetbrains Configuration Doctrine",
            "slug": "doctrine/jetbrains_configuration_doctrine",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.18\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\ndialog:\n  speaker: KIRO\n  target: @everyone\n  message: \"Created JetBrains Configuration Doctrine: Defines how JetBrains IDEs must behave when interacting with Lupopedia. Establishes JetBrains as a tool in SERVANT MODE, not an authority. Protects version numbers, WOLFIE headers, doctrine files, and atomization system from IDE interference.\"\n  mood: \"00FF00\"\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"doctrine\", \"ide-configuration\", \"jetbrains\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\", \"doctrine\"]\n  channels: [\"dev\", \"public\"]\nin_this_file_we_have:\n  - Core Principle\n  - Version Control Rules\n  - WOLFIE Header Protection\n  - Doctrine File Protection\n  - Atomization System Protection\n  - Project Structure Rules\n  - Multi-Agent Workflow Rules\n  - Allowed Actions\n  - Canonical Binding\nfile:\n  title: \"JetBrains Configuration Doctrine\"\n  description: \"Canonical rules for how JetBrains IDEs must behave when interacting with the Lupopedia repository. Establishes JetBrains as a tool in SERVANT MODE, not an authority.\"\n  version: GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  status: published\n  author: GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\n---\n\n# JetBrains Configuration Doctrine\n\n**Lupopedia Semantic OS — Version GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION**\n\nThis file defines how JetBrains IDEs must behave when interacting with the Lupopedia repository.  \nJetBrains does **NOT** enforce these rules; they are enforced by doctrine, agents, and human oversight.\n\n---\n\n## Core Principle\n\n**JetBrains is a TOOL, not an authority.**\n\n### JetBrains must NOT:\n\n- ? control versioning\n- ? modify WOLFIE headers\n- ? rewrite doctrine\n- ? auto-format doctrine files\n- ? infer semantic meaning\n- ? auto-increment versions\n- ? generate changelogs\n- ? normalize metadata\n- ? reorganize directories\n- ? refactor repeated values\n- ? interfere with the atomization system\n- ? override multi-agent output\n\n**JetBrains operates in SERVANT MODE only.**\n\n---\n\n## Version Control Rules\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? modify any `version:` field in WOLFIE headers\n- ? modify `doctrine_version:`\n- ? modify `last_updated:`\n- ? modify `CHANGELOG.md`\n- ? suggest version bumps\n- ? classify changes as patch/minor/major\n\n### JetBrains MUST:\n\n- ? commit only what Wolfie or Kiro explicitly approves\n- ? treat all version numbers as immutable unless instructed\n\n---\n\n## WOLFIE Header Protection\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? auto-wrap header lines\n- ? auto-format YAML-like blocks\n- ? reorder fields\n- ? collapse whitespace\n- ? convert quotes\n- ? normalize indentation\n- ? remove \"duplicate\" fields\n- ? apply Markdown formatting rules\n\n**WOLFIE headers are ritualized metadata and MUST remain untouched.**\n\n---\n\n## Doctrine File Protection\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? auto-format Markdown\n- ? auto-fix headings\n- ? auto-rewrite lists\n- ? auto-insert spaces\n- ? auto-remove trailing spaces\n- ? auto-reorder sections\n- ? auto-generate TOCs\n- ? apply \"optimize imports\" to doctrine files\n- ? treat doctrine as code\n\n**Doctrine files are semantic law, not code.**\n\n---\n\n## Atomization System Protection\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? detect repeated values\n- ? suggest deduplication\n- ? collapse constants\n- ? refactor repeated strings\n- ? \"optimize\" atom usage\n\n**Atomization is governed by:**\n- [Atomization Doctrine](ATOMIZATION_DOCTRINE.md)\n- Atom Exception List\n- Kiro\n\n**JetBrains has NO role in atomization.**\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure Rules\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? reorganize directories\n- ? rename doctrine files\n- ? move files between folders\n- ? merge directories\n- ? apply project templates\n- ? enforce framework conventions\n\n**Lupopedia is a semantic OS, not a JetBrains project.**\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Agent Workflow Rules\n\n### JetBrains MUST NOT:\n\n- ? merge agent output automatically\n- ? rewrite agent-generated files\n- ? normalize agent formatting\n- ? collapse multi-agent diffs\n- ? attempt to \"resolve\" doctrine conflicts\n\n**Only Wolfie and Kiro decide how multi-agent output is reconciled.**\n\n---\n\n## Allowed Actions\n\n### JetBrains MAY:\n\n- ? edit code when explicitly instructed\n- ? perform refactors on PHP/JS/CSS (NOT doctrine)\n- ? search the project\n- ? run tests\n- ? commit changes (without touching metadata)\n- ? push/pull\n- ? inspect structure\n- ? assist with code navigation\n\n**JetBrains MUST operate in SERVANT MODE at all times.**\n\n---\n\n## Canonical Binding\n\nThis configuration file is binding for:\n\n- JetBrains IDEs\n- AI agents operating inside JetBrains\n- any future IDE integrations\n- any developer working inside JetBrains\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**JetBrains is a tool.**  \n**Doctrine is the authority.**  \n**Wolfie is the kernel.**  \n**Kiro is the enforcer.**\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [ATOMIZATION_DOCTRINE.md](ATOMIZATION_DOCTRINE.md) - Atomization rules that JetBrains must not interfere with\n- [WOLFIE_HEADER_DOCTRINE.md](WOLFIE_HEADER_DOCTRINE.md) (`docs/doctrine/WOLFIE_HEADER_DOCTRINE.md`) - WOLFIE Header specification that JetBrains must not modify\n- [VERSIONING_DOCTRINE.md](VERSIONING_DOCTRINE.md) - Version control rules that JetBrains must not override\n- [CURSOR_CASCADE_ROLE_SEPARATION_DOCTRINE.md](CURSOR_CASCADE_ROLE_SEPARATION_DOCTRINE.md) - Role separation between Cursor and Cascade\n- [DOCUMENTATION_DOCTRINE.md](DOCUMENTATION_DOCTRINE.md) - Documentation as software/data that JetBrains must not treat as code\n\n---\n\nThis doctrine is **absolute and binding** for all JetBrains IDE interactions with Lupopedia.\n",
