            "body": "---\narchitect: Captain Wolfie\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.15\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\ndialog:\n  speaker: \"CASCADE\"\n  target: \"@everyone\"\n  mood_RGB: \"00FF00\"\n  message: \"Created Doctrines README v1.0 - index of all Lupopedia doctrinal documents\"\ntags:\n  categories: [\"documentation\", \"index\", \"doctrine\"]\n  collections: [\"core-docs\", \"doctrine\"]\n  channels: [\"public\", \"dev\", \"standards\"]\nfile:\n  title: \"Lupopedia Doctrines README v1.0\"\n  description: \"Index and overview of all Lupopedia doctrinal documents and specifications\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  status: published\n  author: \"Captain Wolfie\"\n---\n\n# ?? **Lupopedia Doctrines README v1.0**  \n*Index and overview of all Lupopedia doctrinal documents and specifications*\n\n---\n\n## ?? 1. Purpose\n\nThis directory contains **mandatory rules and non-negotiable principles** that govern the Lupopedia ecosystem. Doctrines define the fundamental architecture, behavior, and standards that all agents, systems, and implementations must follow.\n\n---\n\n## ?? 2. Doctrine Categories\n\n### Core Doctrines\n\nFundamental principles that define the Lupopedia ecosystem:\n\n- **Universal Wolfie Header Specification** - Minimal universal metadata standard\n- **Lupopedia Header Profile** - Expressive metadata extensions\n- **Mood System Doctrine** - Multi-dimensional emotional representation\n- **Color Doctrine** - RGB mapping for emotional visualization\n\n### Protocol Specifications\n\nDetailed implementation protocols for specific operations:\n\n- **Mood Calculation Protocol** - Deterministic emotional computation\n- **Thread Aggregation Protocol** - Emotional accumulation across conversations\n- **RGB Mapping Protocol** - Color-based emotional representation\n\n### Registries\n\nGoverned lists and definitions that prevent drift:\n\n- **Mood Axis Registry** - Canonical emotional axis definitions\n- **Additional registries** - For other governed taxonomies\n\n---\n\n## ?? 3. Document Relationships\n\n### Hierarchy\n\n```\nUniversal Wolfie Header Specification (WHS)\n+-- Lupopedia Header Profile (LHP)\n    +-- Required Fields (dialog, authorship, sections)\n    +-- Optional Fields (file, tags, placement, etc.)\n    +-- Mood System Extensions\n        +-- Mood System Doctrine (Framework)\n        +-- Mood Axis Registry (Definitions)\n        +-- RGB Mapping Protocol (Colors)\n        +-- Mood Calculation Protocol (Algorithms)\n        +-- Thread Aggregation Protocol (Analysis)\n```\n\n### Integration Points\n\n- **WHS** provides universal foundation\n- **LHP** extends WHS with Lupopedia-specific metadata\n- **Mood System** provides emotional representation capabilities\n- **Protocols** define specific implementation requirements\n- **Registries** maintain canonical definitions\n\n---\n\n## ?? 4. Implementation Requirements\n\n### Mandatory Compliance\n\nAll implementations must:\n\n- **Follow WHS** for universal header compatibility\n- **Implement LHP** for Lupopedia-specific metadata\n- **Use Mood System** for emotional representation\n- **Follow Protocols** for specific operations\n- **Reference Registries** for canonical definitions\n\n### Validation Requirements\n\n- **Header validation** for WHS/LHP compliance\n- **Mood validation** for emotional representation\n- **Protocol validation** for operation correctness\n- **Registry compliance** for definition usage\n\n---\n\n## ?? 5. Prohibited Operations\n\n### No Doctrine Modification\n\nImplementations must **not**:\n- Modify core doctrine principles\n- Create alternative protocol versions\n- Use non-canonical axis definitions\n- Ignore mandatory header requirements\n\n### No Bypass Procedures\n\nSystems must **not**:\n- Skip validation requirements\n- Use deprecated protocol versions\n- Override registry definitions\n- Implement partial doctrine compliance\n\n---\n\n## ?? 6. January 2026 Doctrine Extensions\n\nThe doctrine layer now includes:\n- **Dual-Channel Affective Stack** (RGB + ATP)\n- **Contextual Resonance Field** (CRF)\n- **Experience Ledger**\n- **Heterodox Engine**\n- **Meta-Governance Extensions**\n- **Doctrine Versioning Support**\n\n### Extension Integration\n\nThese extensions enhance the existing doctrine framework while maintaining compatibility with core principles. All extensions are documented in their respective specification files and integrated through the established header and metadata systems.\n\n---\n\n## ?? 7. Implementation Resources\n\n### Core Documents\n\n- **Universal Wolfie Header Specification**: `UNIVERSAL_WOLFIE_HEADER_SPECIFICATION.md`\n- **Lupopedia Header Profile**: `LUPOPEDIA_HEADER_PROFILE.md`\n- **Mood System Doctrine**: `MOOD_SYSTEM_DOCTRINE.md`\n- **Color Doctrine**: `COLOR_DOCTRINE.md`\n\n### Protocol Documents\n\n- **Mood Calculation Protocol**: `MOOD_CALCULATION_PROTOCOL.md`\n- **Thread Aggregation Protocol**: `THREAD_AGGREGATION_PROTOCOL.md`\n- **RGB Mapping Protocol**: `COLOR_DOCTRINE.md` (integrated)\n\n### Registry Documents\n\n- **Mood Axis Registry**: `../registries/MOOD_AXIS_REGISTRY.md`\n- **Additional Registries**: Located in `../registries/`\n\n### System Documents\n\n- **Experience Ledger**: `../systems/EXPERIENCE_LEDGER.md`\n- **Heterodox Engine**: `../systems/HETERODOX_ENGINE.md`\n- **CRF Specification**: `../systems/CRF_SPECIFICATION.md`\n- **Affective Discrepancy Engine**: `../systems/AFFECTIVE_DISCREPANCY_ENGINE.md`\n\n---\n\n## ?? 8. Scope and Versioning\n\nThis is **Doctrines README v1.0** (January 2026).\n\nIt applies to all Lupopedia doctrinal documents and their relationships.\n\nFuture versions may add new doctrines or modify organizational structure, but core principles are immutable.\n\n---\n\n*Last Updated: January 13, 2026*  \n*Version: 1.0.0*  \n*Author: Captain Wolfie*  \n*Canonical Reference: https://lupopedia.com/what/doctrines*\n",
