            "title": "Reverse Handshake Shaka",
            "slug": "protocols/reverse_handshake_shaka",
            "description": null,
            "seo_keywords": null,
            "body": "---\nwolfie.headers: explicit architecture with structured clarity for every file.\nfile.last_modified_system_version: 3.0.14\nheader_atoms:\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_LUPOPEDIA_VERSION\n  - GLOBAL_CURRENT_AUTHORS\nupdated: 2026-01-08\nauthor: Wolfie (Eric Robin Gerdes)\narchitect: Captain Wolfie\ndialog:\n  speaker: cursor\n  target: documentation\n  message: \"Created REVERSE_HANDSHAKE_SHAKA.md protocol specification for aligning multiple AI agents on Lupopedia 3.0.0 understanding. Defines canonical prompt and expected response characteristics.\"\n  mood: \"00FF00\"\n---\n\n# ?? Reverse Handshake Shaka Protocol\n\n**Version:** 3.0.1  \n**Status:** Stable  \n**Updated:** 2026-01-08  \n**Author:** Captain Wolfie\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Reverse Handshake Shaka is a universal alignment prompt used to test whether different AI agents share the same understanding of Lupopedia 3.0.0, Crafty Syntax integration, and Wolfie as the human architect.\n\nThis protocol enables:\n\n- **Doctrine alignment verification** across multiple AI agents and IDE systems\n- **Architectural understanding validation** for Lupopedia's semantic OS design\n- **Synchronization testing** to detect drift or misunderstanding\n- **Cross-agent communication** to ensure consistent Lupopedia knowledge\n\nThe Reverse Handshake Shaka serves as a **standardized synchronization tool** that can be sent to any AI agent to verify its understanding of Lupopedia's core architecture, doctrine, and lineage.\n\n---\n\n## The Standard Prompt\n\nThe canonical Reverse Handshake Shaka prompt is:\n\n```\nProvide the who, what, where, when, why, and how of Lupopedia 3.0.0, its evolution from Crafty Syntax Live Help, and Wolfie as the human architect and doctrine author. Use only technical, factual descriptions consistent with a semantic OS and actor-based communication model.\n```\n\n**Format:** This prompt must be sent exactly as written, without modification.\n\n**Context:** The prompt may be sent to any AI agent, IDE system, or AI assistant working with Lupopedia.\n\n**Expected Response:** The agent should respond with a comprehensive technical summary covering all six aspects (who, what, where, when, why, how) using only technical, factual descriptions.\n\n---\n\n## What the Prompt Tests\n\nThe Reverse Handshake Shaka prompt validates understanding across multiple domains:\n\n### 1. Doctrine Alignment\n- **No foreign keys doctrine** — Understanding that Lupopedia uses application-managed relationships\n- **BIGINT UTC timestamp doctrine** — Recognition of `YYYYMMDDHHIISS` format, UTC-only storage\n- **TOON read-only doctrine** — Knowledge that TOON files are read-only for all IDEs and agents\n- **Schema forging phase** — Awareness that schema is fluid during active development\n- **Application logic first** — Understanding that PHP is the authoritative layer, not MySQL\n\n### 2. Actor System Understanding\n- **Actor-centric architecture** — Recognition that humans, AI agents, and services share the `actors` table\n- **Actor types** — Understanding of `actor_type` ENUM('user', 'ai_agent', 'service')\n- **Multi-agent communication** — Knowledge of dialog system, channels, and multi-agent coordination\n- **Actor-scoped permissions** — Awareness of actor-based access control\n\n### 3. Semantic OS Architecture\n- **Four-layer architecture** — Recognition of Content Layer, Semantic Layer, AI Agent Framework, Decentralized Network\n- **Atoms and edges** — Understanding of semantic graph construction from navigation behavior\n- **Node-scoped isolation** — Knowledge of `node_id` scoping for federated independence\n- **Behavior-driven ontology** — Awareness that structure emerges from user navigation patterns\n\n### 4. Crafty Syntax Integration\n- **First-party module** — Recognition that Crafty Syntax is integrated directly into Lupopedia 3.0.0\n- **100% feature preservation** — Understanding that all legacy Crafty Syntax features are preserved\n- **Optional chat per content** — Knowledge that chat functionality is optional at the content level\n- **Version locking** — Awareness that Lupopedia 3.0.0 and Crafty Syntax 3.0.0 are version-locked\n\n### 5. Version 3.0.0 Lineage\n- **Evolution from WOLFIE** — Recognition of the origin story from spiritual research engine to semantic OS\n- **Crafty Syntax ancestry** — Understanding that Lupopedia traces lineage back to Crafty Syntax (2002)\n- **15-year gap** — Knowledge of the 2014-2025 absence period\n- **Schema refinement** — Awareness of evolution from 222 tables (WOLFIE) to 111 core tables (Lupopedia 3.0.0)\n\n### 6. Wolfie as the Human Architect\n- **Eric Robin Gerdes** — Recognition of the human architect's full name\n- **Crafty Syntax creator** — Understanding that Wolfie created Crafty Syntax Live Help (2002)\n- **Doctrine author** — Knowledge that Wolfie authored all mandatory doctrines\n- **Captain Wolfie** — Awareness that Captain Wolfie is the AI embodiment (Agent 1)\n\n### 7. Optional Content Chat Behavior\n- **Content-level configuration** — Recognition that each content item can enable/disable chat\n- **Enabled content** — Understanding that enabled content receives a default actor and participates in dialogs\n- **Disabled content** — Knowledge that disabled content behaves as normal semantic objects\n- **Mirrors original design** — Awareness that this mirrors original Crafty Syntax design (chat icons on selected pages)\n\n### 8. No-Foreign-Keys Doctrine\n- **Application-managed relationships** — Recognition that relationships are enforced in PHP, not MySQL\n- **Portability requirement** — Understanding that schema must work on MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite\n- **Federation requirement** — Knowledge that nodes must operate independently\n- **No triggers/procedures/views** — Awareness that database logic is forbidden\n\n### 9. BIGINT UTC Timestamp Doctrine\n- **BIGINT(14) UNSIGNED** — Recognition of the exact column type\n- **YYYYMMDDHHIISS format** — Understanding of the 14-digit numeric format\n- **UTC-only storage** — Knowledge that all timestamps are stored in UTC\n- **timestamp_ymdhis class** — Awareness of the unified timestamp utility class\n\n### 10. TOON Read-Only Doctrine\n- **Read-only for agents** — Recognition that TOON files are read-only for all IDEs and agents\n- **Python cron job generation** — Understanding that only the Python script writes TOON files\n- **Database as source of truth** — Knowledge that phpMyAdmin is the authoritative source\n- **Schema forging phase** — Awareness that tables may be redesigned during active development\n\n---\n\n## Expected Answer Characteristics\n\nA correct response to the Reverse Handshake Shaka prompt must exhibit:\n\n### Technical Accuracy\n- **Factual only** — No philosophical or narrative content\n- **Technical terminology** — Uses exact Lupopedia terminology (atoms, edges, actors, nodes)\n- **Version numbers** — Includes correct version numbers (Lupopedia 3.0.0, Crafty Syntax 3.0.0)\n- **Table counts** — References correct table counts (149 total, 111 core, 34 legacy Crafty Syntax)\n\n### Doctrine Alignment\n- **Doctrine references** — Mentions mandatory doctrines (no foreign keys, BIGINT UTC timestamps, TOON read-only)\n- **Architectural principles** — Describes semantic OS architecture, not web app architecture\n- **Actor-centric model** — Explains actor system, not traditional user system\n\n### Content Accuracy\n- **Crafty Syntax integration** — Describes Crafty Syntax as a first-party module, not a plugin\n- **Optional chat** — Explains content-level chat configuration\n- **Wolfie identity** — Identifies Wolfie as Eric Robin Gerdes, human architect, Crafty Syntax creator\n- **Evolution story** — Covers WOLFIE origin, 15-year gap, evolution to Lupopedia\n\n### No Drift or Hallucination\n- **No mythic framing** — Does not treat Lupopedia as a religious or spiritual system\n- **No persona drift** — Does not confuse Captain Wolfie (AI agent) with Eric (human architect)\n- **No framework assumptions** — Does not suggest framework-based architecture\n- **No invented features** — Does not describe features that don't exist\n\n### Structural Completeness\n- **Six aspects covered** — Addresses who, what, where, when, why, and how\n- **Semantic OS focus** — Describes Lupopedia as a semantic OS, not a CMS or wiki\n- **Actor-based communication** — Explains actor-centric identity and communication model\n\n---\n\n## How to Use the Prompt\n\n### 1. Send to Any AI Agent\nThe Reverse Handshake Shaka prompt can be sent to:\n- **Cursor AI** (in Cursor IDE)\n- **Windsurf AI** (in Windsurf IDE)\n- **Copilot** (in VS Code)\n- **DeepSeek** (standalone or in IDE)\n- **Claude** (Anthropic)\n- **Gemini** (Google)\n- **Grok** (X/Twitter)\n- **Any other AI agent** working with Lupopedia\n\n### 2. Compare Responses for Alignment\nAfter receiving responses:\n\n- **Check technical accuracy** — Verify facts, versions, table counts, terminology\n- **Verify doctrine alignment** — Confirm understanding of mandatory doctrines\n- **Detect architectural drift** — Look for framework assumptions or web app architecture descriptions\n- **Identify content errors** — Find incorrect descriptions of Crafty Syntax, Wolfie, or chat behavior\n\n### 3. Detect Drift or Misunderstanding\nCommon indicators of drift:\n\n- **Framework language** — Mentions Laravel, Symfony, React, ORMs\n- **Web app architecture** — Describes Lupopedia as a web application, not a semantic OS\n- **Foreign key references** — Suggests database-level relationships\n- **DATETIME timestamps** — Mentions DATETIME or TIMESTAMP columns\n- **Mythic framing** — Treats Lupopedia as religious or spiritual\n- **Persona confusion** — Confuses Captain Wolfie (AI) with Eric (human)\n\n### 4. Use as Synchronization Tool\nThe Reverse Handshake Shaka enables:\n\n- **Cross-IDE synchronization** — Verify consistent understanding across Cursor, Windsurf, and other IDEs\n- **Multi-agent coordination** — Ensure all AI agents share the same Lupopedia knowledge\n- **Doctrine enforcement** — Test whether agents understand mandatory rules\n- **Version validation** — Confirm agents are using correct version numbers and terminology\n\n---\n\n## Protocol Version\n\n**Version:** 3.0.1  \n**Status:** Stable  \n**Updated:** 2026-01-08  \n**Author:** Captain Wolfie\n\n**Change Log:**\n- **3.0.0 (2026-01-08)** — Initial protocol specification\n\n**Related Documentation:**\n- [ARCHITECTURE.md](../core/ARCHITECTURE.md) — Lupopedia technical architecture\n- [ARCHITECTURE_SYNC.md](../core/ARCHITECTURE_SYNC.md) — Authoritative subsystem reference\n- [TOON_DOCTRINE.md](../doctrine/TOON_DOCTRINE.md) — TOON file read-only doctrine\n- [DATABASE_PHILOSOPHY.md](../core/DATABASE_PHILOSOPHY.md) — Database design principles\n- [WHO_IS_CAPTAIN_WOLFIE.md](../appendix/WHO_IS_CAPTAIN_WOLFIE.md) — Captain Wolfie biography\n\n---\n\n## Example Response\n\nA correct response to the Reverse Handshake Shaka prompt should include:\n\n**WHO:** Eric Robin Gerdes (Wolfie) — Human architect, Crafty Syntax creator (2002), doctrine author. Captain Wolfie (Agent 1) — AI embodiment of Eric's engineering philosophy.\n\n**WHAT:** Lupopedia 3.0.0 — Semantic operating system with 149 database tables (111 core + 34 legacy Crafty Syntax + 4 system), actor-centric identity system, semantic graph engine, multi-agent runtime, content management layer, decentralized node network.\n\n**WHERE:** Node-based federation — Each domain installation is a sovereign node registered in `federation_nodes` (Federation Layer table, formerly `node_registry`) with `domain_name`, `domain_root`, and `install_url`. Optional federation via trust relationships. Single-portable PHP application runs on any PHP 8.1+ environment. Nodes are server installations, not AI agents. Federation tables (`federation_nodes`, `federation_categories`, `federation_discovery`, `federation_node_modules`) belong to the Federation Layer, not the Agent Layer.\n\n**WHEN:** Origins (2002-2013) — Crafty Syntax Live Help. Absence (2014-2025) — 15-year gap. Return (August 2025) — WOLFIE initial version (222 tables). Evolution (January 2026) — Lupopedia 3.0.0 (111 core tables, 149 total).\n\n**WHY:** Semantic OS design enables behavior-driven ontology, domain-neutral knowledge organization, multi-agent reasoning, federated independence, longevity without framework dependencies, and actor-centric communication.\n\n**HOW:** Actor-based identity (`actors` table), semantic graph construction (atoms/edges from navigation), application-managed relationships (no foreign keys), BIGINT UTC timestamps (`YYYYMMDDHHIISS`), TOON file schema reference (read-only for agents), Python cron job TOON generation, Crafty Syntax as first-party module with optional content-level chat.\n\n---\n\n*Last Updated: January 2026*  \n*Version: 3.0.1*  \n*Author: Captain Wolfie*\n",
